lessons:
  id: L139
  rule: "Documentation cross-audit must distinguish W9 scope from pre-existing workspace debt"
  source: 2026-06-11 W9 Documentation Cross-Audit (D4 finding)
  detail: |
    A documentation deliverable's cross-audit should focus on the
    DOCUMENTATION artifacts created/modified in that wave. Code-level
    issues (e.g., broken examples) that pre-date the wave are out of
    scope per L135 (bounded audit discipline). Document them in
    `do_not_ship` for the next-version backlog rather than expanding
    the audit's fix surface.

  id: L140
  rule: "When updating docs that reference future waves, mark them complete when shipped"
  source: 2026-06-11 W9 Documentation Cross-Audit (D2 finding)
  detail: |
    When a documentation deliverable introduces a 'wave' entry as TBD
    in a status table, the cross-audit must verify the wave shipped
    and update the entry to ✅. Leaving TBD creates a "planned but not
    built" violation of the audit's "nothing pending" rule.

  id: L141
  rule: "mkdocs build --strict is the source of truth for nav validity, not regex scripts"
  source: 2026-06-11 W9 Documentation Cross-Audit (Phase 4)
  detail: |
    A regex-based "verify all nav entries resolve" script can produce
    false positives (61 'missing' entries in our case). mkdocs build
    --strict, with its 0-warning output, is the authoritative validator.
    Custom analysis scripts should report ONLY findings not already
    covered by mkdocs build --strict.

do_not_ship:
  - 2_example_compilation_errors: "examples/02_citation_graph.rs and examples/04_doc_generation.rs reference kazuba_rust_core::error::KazubaResult which no longer exists in the post-W2 multi-crate workspace. Out of W9 scope (L139). Defer to v3.2.0 example refactor."
  - 2_faq_anchor_mismatches: "Anchor links in faq.md use old heading slugs. mkdocs --strict does not block (INFO only). Minor fix candidate for v3.2.0."

